+
+World-model startup first checks the current schema capability. Only the schema
+owner (or a member of that owner role) with schema `CREATE` enters the migration
+path. A long-lived runtime role with schema `USAGE` and no `CREATE` instead
+performs a read-only admission check: `schema_migrations` must be an exact,
+separately owned, `SELECT`-only ledger with every expected version through v38.
+Missing or stale migrations require rerunning the owner job; a changed ledger
+shape, ownership boundary, privilege set, constraint, index, or row fails
+startup as incompatible. The runtime path never creates or advances the
+migration ledger. Apply the ledger `REVOKE` after every future broad table-grant
+refresh.
+
+The v34 migration owns both promotion tables and the append-only trigger
+function under the migration owner and revokes their default `PUBLIC` grants.
+Runtime admission verifies that common owner, the absence of owner membership
+and database/schema `CREATE` or database `TEMP`, and the exact effective
+table/function ACLs on every promotion transaction. Revoking `TEMP` prevents a
+runtime session from shadowing ledger relations through `pg_temp`. A
+runtime-created or runtime-owned promotion schema is refused. Future schema
