+
+The v37 queue admission gate applies the same owner/runtime separation. It also
+pins database, schema, and role identity; table and identity-sequence
+persistence; column order, defaults, generated identity, primary/check
+definitions; validated and ready indexes; absence of triggers, rewrite rules,
+and inheritance; RLS policy; exact table/sequence privileges; absence of grant
+options, public ACLs, and column ACLs; and the identity sequence parameters.
+Missing queue DDL is never created by the runtime: rerun the migration job and
+reviewed grants instead.
+
+The v36/v38 canonical-audit gate separately requires `SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE` on
+`canonical_audit_heads`, `SELECT, INSERT` on `canonical_audit_events`, and no
+runtime/public execution of its append-only rejection function. Signer trust
+requires `SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE` on `canonical_audit_signers` and
+`canonical_audit_signer_state`, with no delete/truncate/grant option. Epoch one
+must be externally digest-pinned before the explicit bootstrap ceremony; later
+keys are staged under a signature from the current key and only activate when
+their first new event proves possession in the same event/head transaction.
+`canonical_audit_signer_recoveries` requires exactly `SELECT, INSERT`; replacing
