+### Strict MCP stdio identity
+
+Strict authority removes the ambient local/operator identity from the MCP
+stdio transport. Configure one attributable inbound Agent Trust principal; the
+server refuses to start if it is absent, synthetic, revoked, expired, unknown,
+or outbound-only. The environment variable
+`MAVERICK_MCP_STDIO_PRINCIPAL` overrides `[mcp] stdio_principal`.
+
+```toml
+[authority]
+mode = "strict"
+
+[mcp]
+stdio_principal = "desktop-copilot"
+
+[agent_trust]
+enforce = true
+
+[[agent_trust.agents]]
+id = "desktop-copilot"
+direction = "inbound"
+allow_tools = ["maverick_start", "maverick_status", "maverick_resume"]
+max_risk = "medium"
+```
+
+The process resolves identity, inbound admission, and capability from one
+registry snapshot at startup. Every stdio tool, resource, subscription, prompt,
+and task operation carries that immutable authority. Queued work rechecks the
+current registry and may be revoked or narrowed, never broadened.
