+The Postgres table uses atomic create and revision compare-and-swap, keeps the
+audit outbox in the same transaction as each logical mutation, seals the
+bounded JSON payload when at-rest encryption is active, and enforces exact
+tenant isolation with forced Row-Level Security. Enterprise mode or
+`MAVERICK_REPLICA_COUNT > 1` refuses local storage, an unavailable DSN, an
+unbound/corrupt tenant, disabled application at-rest encryption, or an
+ambiguous RLS policy. Every replica must resolve the same KMS/key material;
+database/volume encryption alone does not satisfy this application-layer
+fleet floor. Connect the application with a least-privilege role that is
+neither a Postgres superuser nor granted `BYPASSRLS`; admission verifies that
+role property. Switching to Postgres also
+refuses to hide existing local records: import them and archive the local
+copies as an explicit cutover step.
