+## Shared canonical audit signer trust
+
+Multi-replica Postgres deployments pin the epoch-one Ed25519 public key and keep
+active private material off-host:
+
+```toml
+[audit]
+sign = true
+require_offhost_key = true
+trust_root_sha256 = "sha256:<64-lowercase-hex>"
+```
+
+Generate the pin with `maverick audit trust-root-digest --public-key <hex>`, then
+run `maverick audit trust-bootstrap`. Later rotations use `maverick audit
+trust-rotate --next-public-key <hex>`; this stages the next public key while the
+old signer remains live. The first event signed by the staged private key
+atomically activates it. Postgres persists only public trust history and signed
+transitions, never private key bytes.
+
+If the staged private half is lost or unusable, do not bootstrap again. The
+current active signer can replace only the exact stranded attempt:
+
+```bash
+maverick audit trust-rotate \
+  --replace-pending-key-id <stranded-key-id> \
+  --next-public-key <replacement-public-hex>
+```
+
+The compare-and-swap ceremony preserves an active-signer-signed, hash-chained
+recovery record in Postgres. A concurrent ceremony naming a different current
+pending key fails closed; the old active signer remains writable until the
+replacement private key proves possession on its first append.
+
